       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as no more than 850 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg BID.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg TID is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose, but I'd advise against it."
